## Context

Quality grounding review (`docs/quality-grounding.md`) gap G1: the
DQAF "coherence" dimension is entirely unmeasured. No check that
extracted capacities sum to known national totals. PDP8 publishes
aggregate thermal capacity by fuel type — these are public numbers.
If a model extracts 163 plants but their total capacity is 20% off
the PDP8 aggregate, something is wrong even if F1 is high.

## Actions

1. Collect PDP8 aggregate thermal capacity by fuel type (coal, gas,
   oil) and by status (operational, construction, planned). These
   are in the PDP8 document already in the RAG corpus.
2. Add a `check_consistency(extracted_df, aggregates)` function that
   compares summed capacity by fuel×status against the known totals.
   Return absolute and percentage differences.
3. Wire into the evaluation pipeline: report consistency alongside
   F1/precision/recall in measurements.
4. Add to the verification reporting: a row showing aggregate
   deviation per fuel type.

## Test

`check_consistency()` on the reference CSV against PDP8 aggregates
returns <5% deviation (the reference is hand-compiled from the same
source). On a known-bad extraction with hallucinated large plants,
deviation is flagged.

## Exit criteria

- Consistency check function implemented and tested
- Reported alongside core metrics for at least one sweep
- Deviation documented in the article's results
